# The First Star

In the beginning, the world existed in eternal twilight—neither bright nor dark, but caught in an endless gray that made all things seem distant and dreamlike.

The Sky Keeper grew lonely watching over this dim realm. She had no companion except her own reflection in the still waters below. One day, she wept, and her tears fell like silver rain. But instead of reaching the earth, each tear froze in the cold upper air, suspended between heaven and ground.

The first tear that fell became the first star, burning with all the loneliness and longing the Sky Keeper had felt. Seeing its beauty, she wept more freely, and soon the heavens filled with countless points of light, each one a crystallized moment of her sorrow transformed into radiance.

The people below saw the stars and felt less alone in the darkness. They began to tell stories, connecting the lights into patterns—hunters and heroes, beasts and legends. The Sky Keeper, hearing their voices drift upward, realized she had never truly been alone.

Now, whenever someone feels isolated in the dark, they need only look up to see the Sky Keeper's gift: proof that even loneliness, when shared, can illuminate the world.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

